  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Local Migration Governance Indicator (MGI) in Dublin City</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM&#x2019;s Migration Governance Indicators (MGI) help governments and local authorities, upon request, take stock of their migration policies and strategies, to identify good practices and areas with potential for further development. By focusing on government ownership of the process, the MGI supports governments and local authorities to improve their migration management systems at national and local levels. This project aims at conducting an MGI assessment for the city of Dublin in Ireland. In order to do so, the project will consist of two main activities: drafting a matrix containing the responses to the 87 questions of the local MGI methodology; and drafting a migration governance profile for the city of Dublin.</narrative>
  </description>
